Print: let an embedder take the output Godot writes to stdout and stderr

Some of Godot's output is written straight to stdout or stderr: whatever
goes through the terminal logger (StdLogger), and the fallback that
print_line, print_raw, print_error and the error macros use before the
OS is initialized, during final cleanup (print_ready false), and while
a print or an error is already being printed. An embedder that routes
Godot's output into its own log can replace the OS loggers once modules
initialize, but the output before that and after cleanup starts still
reaches stdio. In a process where only the host's log is collected, it
is lost: for example, an error loading the main pack.

Add set_stdio_print_func(). When a function is set, those paths hand it
the text they would have written, newlines included, typed as output,
error or warning, instead of writing it. The error fallback puts each
error and its location on one line. The Unix terminal logger leaves out
its color codes. Without a function, the output is unchanged.

The ihs module sets it in the bridge's configure(), before the engine
is created, when the host passes an engine_log callback.

Applied by godot/CMakeLists.txt on top of GODOT_GIT_REF, after 0005.

